Advisory A3 (radical innovation, do not apply in this run): use one writer for the `swapped` status. Today three places write `swapped`: the end of phase B and both branches of `_finish_swap`. The backfill would be a fourth. Add one `_mark_swapped(home, record, *, now) -> bool` that copies the record, sets `status = "swapped"` and `swapped_at = now`, and calls `_write_outcome`. Phase B, both `_finish_swap` branches, and the stop-path backfill all call it. The backfill is then "a swapped record with no soak time is marked swapped again at `now`". A later writer of `swapped` cannot leave out the soak clock, and the late-resume bug cannot come back through a new write site. The cost is one small helper, and three inline `dict(...)` / `status` assignments go away.
